.TH WILE 1 "October 2026" "wile 0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wile \- prescriptive task dispatcher for Ruby gem projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wile
[\fItask\fR [\fIargs\fR...]] [:\fIoptions\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBWile\fR is a prescriptive task dispatcher for Ruby gem projects,
built around a living project template.
.PP
It scaffolds new projects from the template, keeps existing ones
aligned with it, and automates workflow steps \-\- gemspec upkeep,
testing, and release.
.SH GET STARTED
.TP
.B wile
Display this manual page.
.TP
.B wile list
List all available tasks.
.TP
.B wile help [\fItask\fR]
Show detailed documentation for task(s).
.TP
.B wile test
Run project test suites.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help summary.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version number.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Apply to all targets.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
Run in check-only mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-config= FILE
Configuration file path.
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Display detailed output.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dump
Dump internal structure or data.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Force execution without safety checks.
.TP
.BI \-\-format= WORD
Output format.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List items.
.TP
.BI \-\-name= WORD
Filter or match by name.
.TP
.BI \-\-output= FILE
Write output to file.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-raw
Raw / unformatted output.
.TP
.B \-\-simulate
Simulate execution without making changes.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-strict
Enable strict mode.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-trace
Trace execution.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Assume yes to confirmation prompts.
.SH TASKS
See \fBwile list\fR for the complete list of tasks, or
\fBwile help <task>\fR for individual task details.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ruby (1),
.BR fish (1),
.BR tmux (1)
